{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator pipeline) submitted a stitch task #5472 for generation-run44 in the go-unix-utils project. The task prompt contains the entire project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, source code, coding standards, execution constitution) but the actual task description says: \"Cobbler measure is calling Claude to propose task 0 for generation generation-run44. This issue will be closed automatically when measure completes.\" The specific coding requirements, files to create/modify, acceptance criteria, and design decisions were NOT explicitly listed in the task section — suggesting the stitch prompt file in `.cobbler/history/` contains the actual work specification. The user then interrupted to request a text-only summary of the conversation.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils/moreutils verified via differential testing\n   - Cobbler-scaffold pipeline: measure (task planning) → stitch (code generation)\n   - Generation run 44 on branch `task/generation-run44-5472`\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binaries against Homebrew GNU reference binaries\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` required in all cmd/ utilities\n   - Package contracts for: testutils (srd001), sys (srd002), format (srd003), hashutil (srd086), sizeparse (srd087), encutil (srd088)\n   - Many SRDs with \"ready\" status requirements not yet implemented, spanning: ts, od, printf, sha224sum, sha384sum, b2sum, cksum, sum, base32, base64, basenc, stat, truncate, link, sync, chmod, chgrp, chown, mkfifo, mknod, nice, nohup, users, who, pinky, shred, chroot, install, tsort, pathchk, test, stty, df, dir, vdir, dircolors, pr, ptx, chronic, pee, vidir\n   - Code status analysis shows many utilities with codestatus \"not started\" including: cat, echo, tac, expand, cut, sha1sum, sha512sum, mktemp, groups, sort, mv, sleep, factor, numfmt, od, printf, and all of releases 09.0 through 15.0\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - All pkg/ source files were provided inline in the prompt:\n     - `pkg/encutil/decode.go` and `pkg/encutil/encode.go` - encoding/decoding utilities\n     - `pkg/format/align.go`, `color.go`, `columns.go`, `humansize.go`, `pad.go` - output formatting\n     - `pkg/hashutil/hashconfig.go` and `hashutil.go` - hash computation and verification\n     - `pkg/sizeparse/parse.go` - human-readable size string parsing\n     - `pkg/sys/fileinfo.go`, `signal.go`, `sigpipe.go`, `stat_darwin.go`, `terminal.go` - syscall abstractions\n     - `pkg/testutils/build.go` and `difftest.go` - differential testing harness\n   - No files were modified or created during this conversation\n   - The latest stitch prompt was identified at: `.cobbler/history/2026-05-22-18-28-18-stitch-prompt.yaml` but was NOT read\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered. Only one bash command was executed before interruption.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - The core problem was identifying what specific work task #5472 requires. The task description references \"measure proposing task 0\" which is ambiguous about whether actual coding work is needed. I attempted to read the latest stitch prompt YAML file to find specific requirements but was interrupted before completing this step. The requirement_states in the prompt show many SRDs with \"ready\" requirements, suggesting the measure phase should select some of these for implementation.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive cobbler stitch task prompt containing all project context, execution constitution, go style constitution, requirement states, package contracts, and task description for #547