{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014wcjQDWGp1MDwcLpTWoEir","type":"tool_result","content":"8499\ttask: |\n8500\t    Follow these steps in order. Complete each step before moving to the next.\n8501\t\n8502\t    1. **Review provided context** — The project_context section above already contains all project documentation, SRDs, source code, shared_protocols, and package_contracts inline in this prompt. Review Required Reading files by scrolling up to find them in project_context — do NOT call the Read, Glob, or Grep tools for any file already present above. The only files you may read with tools are files NOT in project_context (e.g. files you are about to create or modify).\n8503\t\n8504\t    2. **Plan approach** — Before writing code, determine:\n8505\t       - What exists already (interfaces, types, patterns in the source code above)\n8506\t       - What patterns to follow (from the provided source code and execution_constitution)\n8507\t       - What the acceptance criteria require\n8508\t\n8509\t    3. **Implement** — Complete the work described in Requirements and Files to Create/Modify. Follow the Design Decisions. Do not deviate from the specified files unless a requirement makes it necessary.\n8510\t\n8511\t    4. **Verify** — Check every item in Acceptance Criteria. Run tests if the criteria require it. Do not skip any criterion.\n8512\tconstraints: |\n8513\t    - Do NOT read any file in the repository to infer style, patterns, or conventions. All style guidance is provided in go_style_constitution above. All source patterns are provided in project_context above. If a file you need is absent from project_context, write it from scratch following go_style_constitution — do not read the filesystem to fill the gap.\n8514\t    - Do NOT use Read, Glob, or Grep tools on files already in project_context. SRDs, source code, ARCHITECTURE, VISION, shared_protocols, package_contracts — all are inline above. Reading them again wastes a turn and adds no information. Only use Read for files not present in project_context.\n8515\t    - Do NOT explore the filesystem. Do NOT run ls, find, tree, or similar commands.\n8516\t    - Do NOT modify files outside the Files to Create/Modify list unless a requirement explicitly demands it.\n8517\t    - Do NOT use bd or cupboard commands. Task tracking is handled externally.\n8518\t    - Do NOT invent interfaces, types, or patterns not described in the source code, Required Reading, or SRDs.\n8519\t    - Do NOT add features, refactoring, or improvements beyond what the requirements specify.\n8520\t    - Do NOT run any git commands. No git add, git commit, git init, git status, rm .git, or any other git operation. Git is managed externally by the orchestrator. Just write code and verify it compiles and passes tests.\n8521\t    - When building cmd/ binaries to verify compilation, use `go build -o bin/<name> ./cmd/<name>/` so outputs land in bin/ (which is git-ignored) rather than in the working directory.\n8522\t    - When a build or lint step fails, read ALL error and warning messages before making any changes. Fix every reported issue in a single edit pass, then run the build once to verify. Do not fix one issue, rebuild, fix the next — batch all fixes into one round.\n8523\t    - When modifying more than 3 locations in the same file, prefer the Write tool (full file replacement) over multiple Edit calls. Each Edit changes the file, invalidating old_string matches for subsequent Edits. Write avoids this by producing the complete file in one call.\n8524\t    - The test suite is the acceptance gate. Do not manually run binaries to compare output against reference implementations. Run `go test` and fix any failures. Manual comparison is only warranted when a test fails and the expected behavior is ambiguous.\n8525\t    - Complete all code changes before running `go build` or `go test`. Do not compile incrementally after each small edit. Mentally verify imports, types, and function signatures, then build once.\n8526\tdescription: |-\n8527\t    deliverable_type: code\n8528\t\n8529\t    required_reading:\n8530\t      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd071-numfmt.yaml (requirements R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R2.4 -- read the full SRD for context)\n8531\t      - cmd/numfmt/main.go (existing implementation from prior task -- extend it)\n8532\t      - cmd/numfmt/numfmt_test.go (existing differential tests from prior task -- extend them)\n8533\t      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing framework -- understand DiffTest and RunDiffTests)\n8534\t\n8535\t    files:\n8536\t      - path: cmd/numfmt/main.go\n8537\t        action: modify\n8538\t        note: Add functionality for srd071 requirements R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R2.4\n8539\t      - path: cmd/numfmt/numfmt_test.go\n8540\t        action: modify\n8541\t        note: Add differential test cases covering R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R2.4\n8542\t\n8543\t    requirements:\n8544\t      - id: R1\n8545\t        text: Implement srd071 requirement R2.1 in cmd/numfmt per the SRD specification\n8546\t      - id: R2\n8547\t        text: Implement srd071 requirement R2.2 in cmd/numfmt per the SRD specification\n8548\t      - id: R3\n8549\t        text: Implement srd071 requirement R2.3 in cmd/numfmt per the SRD specification\n8550\t      - id: R4\n8551\t        text: Implement srd071 requirement R2.4 in cmd/numfmt per the SRD specification\n8552\t\n8553\t    design_decisions:\n8554\t      - id: D1\n8555\t        text: Extend the existing cmd/numfmt implementation -- do not rewrite or restructure existing code. Add only the logic needed for R2.1 through R2.4.\n8556\t      - id: D2\n8557\t        text: Use the differential testing pattern with pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests comparing against the gnumfmt reference binary. All test cases set LC_ALL=C.\n8558\t      - id: D3\n8559\t        text: Skip differential tests if the reference binary gnumfmt is not found via exec.LookPath (t.Skip pattern).\n8560\t\n8561\t    acceptance_criteria:\n8562\t      - id: AC1\n8563\t        text: srd071 R2.1 is implemented and has at least one differential test case exercising it\n8564\t      - id: AC2\n8565\t        text: srd071 R2.2 is implemented and has at least one differential test case exercising it\n8566\t      - id: AC3\n8567\t        text: srd071 R2.3 is implemented and has at least one differential test case exercising it\n8568\t      - id: AC4\n8569\t        text: srd071 R2.4 is implemented and has at least one differential test case exercising it\n8570\t      - id: AC5\n8571\t        text: go build ./cmd/numfmt/ succeeds with no errors\n8572\t      - id: AC6\n8573\t        text: go vet ./cmd/numfmt/ reports no issues\n8574\t      - id: AC7\n8575\t        text: go test ./cmd/numfmt/... -count=1 passes (or skips gracefully if gnumfmt reference binary is not installed)\n8576\tshared_protocols:\n8577\t    - name: Differential testing\n8578\t      description: |\n8579\t        Every cmd/ package verifies its implementation by running the Go binary and the\n8580\t        Homebrew GNU reference binary side by side and comparing stdout, stderr, and exit\n8581\t        code via pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests. Test cases are defined as []testutils.DiffTest\n8582\t        slices in <utility>_test.go files. The harness sets LC_ALL=C by default.\n8583\t      pattern: |\n8584\t        func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n8585\t            goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n8586\t            refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"g<utility>\")\n8587\t            if err != nil { t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\") }\n8588\t            tests := []testutils.DiffTest{ ... }\n8589\t            testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n8590\t        }\n8591\t    - name: Graceful skip on missing reference binary\n8592\t      description: |\n8593\t        All cmd/ test files call exec.LookPath for the Homebrew reference binary at the\n8594\t        start of TestDiff and call t.Skip if it is not found. This allows the test suite\n8595\t        to run on machines without Homebrew GNU binaries installed without reporting false\n8596\t        failures. The binary is never installed by the test itself.\n8597\t      pattern: |\n8598\t        refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"g<utility>\")\n8599\t        if err != nil { t.Skipf(\"reference binary g<utility> not in PATH: %v\", err) }\n8600\t    - name: SIGPIPE handling\n8601\t      description: |\n8602\t        All cmd/ utilities that write to stdout call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at\n8603\t        the start of main. This ensures the process exits 0 when piped output is consumed\n8604\t        by a downstream consumer that closes its stdin (e.g., head, grep -q), matching GNU\n8605\t        coreutils behavior.\n8606\t      pattern: |\n8607\t        func main() {\n8608\t            sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n8609\t            ...\n8610\t        }\n8611\tpackage_contracts:\n8612\t    - srd_id: srd001-testutils\n8613\t      contract:\n8614\t        exports:\n8615\t            - name: DiffTest\n8616\t              signature: type DiffTest struct { Name string; Args []string; Stdin []byte; Env []string; WorkDir string; ExitCode int; Normalize []NormalizeFunc; ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte }\n8617\t            - name: NormalizeFunc\n8618\t              signature: type NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\n8619\t            - name: RunDiffTests\n8620\t              signature: func RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n8621\t            - name: ComposeNormalizers\n8622\t              signature: func ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc\n8623\t            - name: TimestampNormalizer\n8624\t              signature: var TimestampNormalizer NormalizeFunc\n8625\t        imports:\n8626\t            - testing\n8627\t            - os\n8628\t            - os/exec\n8629\t        import_constraints:\n8630\t            - Must not import any cmd/ package.\n8631\t            - Must not import