s set LC_ALL=C.\n      - id: D3\n        text: Skip differential tests if the reference binary gnumfmt is not found via exec.LookPath (t.Skip pattern).\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: srd071 R2.1 is implemented and has at least one differential test case exercising it\n      - id: AC2\n        text: srd071 R2.2 is implemented and has at least one differential test case exercising it\n      - id: AC3\n        text: srd071 R2.3 is implemented and has at least one differential test case exercising it\n      - id: AC4\n        text: srd071 R2.4 is implemented and has at least one differential test case exercising it\n      - id: AC5\n        text: go build ./cmd/numfmt/ succeeds with no errors\n      - id: AC6\n        text: go vet ./cmd/numfmt/ reports no issues\n      - id: AC7\n        text: go test ./cmd/numfmt/... -count=1 passes (or skips gracefully if gnumfmt reference binary is not installed)\nshared_protocols:\n    - name: Differential testing\n      description: |\n        Every cmd/ package verifies its implementation by running the Go binary and the\n        Homebrew GNU reference binary side by side and comparing stdout, stderr, and exit\n        code via pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests. Test cases are defined as []testutils.DiffTest\n        slices in <utility>_test.go files. The harness sets LC_ALL=C by default.\n      pattern: |\n        func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n            goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n            refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"g<utility>\")\n            if err != nil { t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\") }\n            tests := []testutils.DiffTest{ ... }\n            testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n        }\n    - name: Graceful skip on missing reference binary\n      description: |\n        All cmd/ test files call exec.LookPath for the Homebrew reference binary at the\n        start of TestDiff and call t.Skip if it is not found. This allows the test suite\n        to run