{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WAKr621bShMQYTWrabajMu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd071-numfmt\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/numfmt: Convert Numbers from/to Human-Readable Strings\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Shell scripts and data pipelines use numfmt to convert numbers between raw numeric values\n6\t  and human-readable formats with SI or IEC suffixes (e.g., 1K, 1Ki, 1M). macOS has no\n7\t  built-in numfmt command. GNU numfmt from coreutils supports input and output format\n8\t  conversion, field selection, padding, and header skipping. The Go implementation must\n9\t  match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gnumfmt, installed by coreutils) in output and\n10\t  exit codes for all supported flag combinations, verified by differential testing via\n11\t  pkg/testutils.\n12\t\n13\tgoals:\n14\t  - G1: Convert numbers between raw numeric and human-readable formats.\n15\t  - G2: Support SI and IEC suffix conventions for both input and output.\n16\t  - G3: Support field selection, padding, and header skipping for tabular data.\n17\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gnumfmt via differential testing.\n18\t\n19\trequirements:\n20\t  R1:\n21\t    title: Default behavior and output conversion\n22\t    items:\n23\t      - R1.1:\n24\t          text: \"When given --to=UNIT, must convert each input number to a human-readable string with the appropriate suffix. UNIT is one of: si (powers of 1000), iec (powers of 1024), iec-i (powers of 1024 with 'i' suffix), or none.\"\n25\t      - R1.2:\n26\t          text: \"When given --from=UNIT, must interpret each input number as a human-readable string with suffixes and convert to a raw number. UNIT values are the same as --to.\"\n27\t      - R1.3:\n28\t          text: When neither --from nor --to is given, must pass numbers through unchanged.\n29\t      - R1.4:\n30\t          text: Must read numbers from stdin (one per line) when no operands are given, or process command-line operands directly.\n31\t\n32\t  R2:\n33\t    title: Format control\n34\t    items:\n35\t      - R2.1:\n36\t          text: \"--format=FORMAT must use a printf-style format string for output (e.g., '%10f', '%.2f'). Must support width, precision, and left-alignment.\"\n37\t      - R2.2:\n38\t          text: \"--padding=N must pad the output to N characters. Positive N right-aligns; negative N left-aligns.\"\n39\t      - R2.3:\n40\t          text: \"--round=METHOD must control rounding: up (ceiling), down (floor), from-zero (away from zero), towards-zero (truncation), or nearest (default).\"\n41\t      - R2.4:\n42\t          text: \"--suffix=SUFFIX must append SUFFIX to the output after the numeric value and any unit suffix.\"\n43\t\n44\t  R3:\n45\t    title: Field selection and header\n46\t    items:\n47\t      - R3.1:\n48\t          text: \"--field=FIELDS must convert only the specified fields (1-indexed, comma-separated ranges like cut). Other fields are passed through unchanged.\"\n49\t      - R3.2:\n50\t          text: \"-d DELIM or --delimiter=DELIM must use DELIM as the field delimiter for --field processing.\"\n51\t      - R3.3:\n52\t          text: \"--header[=N] must pass through the first N lines (default 1) without conversion, treating them as headers.\"\n53\t      - R3.4:\n54\t          text: \"--to-unit=N must scale the output by dividing by N before applying --to conversion. --from-unit=N must scale the input by multiplying by N before applying --from conversion.\"\n55\t\n56\t  R4:\n57\t    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n58\t    items:\n59\t      - R4.1:\n60\t          text: Must exit 0 when all conversions complete successfully.\n61\t      - R4.2:\n62\t          text: Must exit 2 when an invalid number is encountered (unless --invalid=ignore or --invalid=warn is set).\n63\t      - R4.3:\n64\t          text: \"Differential tests must compare stdout and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils.\"\n65\t      - R4.4:\n66\t          text: \"Tests must cover: --to si/iec/iec-i, --from si/iec, --format with width and precision, --padding, --round modes, --suffix, --field selection, --delimiter, --header, --to-unit/--from-unit, stdin and operand input, and error cases (invalid number, unknown suffix).\"\n67\t\n68\tnon_goals:\n69\t  - cmd/numfmt does not implement locale-aware digit grouping (e.g., thousands separators).\n70\t  - cmd/numfmt does not implement --grouping.\n71\t\n72\tacceptance_criteria:\n73\t  - id: AC1\n74\t    criterion: \"echo 1048576 | go run ./cmd/numfmt --to=iec produces '1.0M', matching gnumfmt.\"\n75\t    traces:\n76\t      - R1.1\n77\t      - R1.4\n78\t  - id: AC2\n79\t    criterion: \"echo 1K | go run ./cmd/numfmt --from=si produces '1000', matching gnumfmt.\"\n80\t    traces:\n81\t      - R1.2\n82\t  - id: AC3\n83\t    criterion: \"echo 1500000 | go run ./cmd/numfmt --to=si --format='%10.2f' produces a right-aligned formatted value, matching gnumfmt.\"\n84\t    traces:\n85\t      - R1.1\n86\t      - R2.1\n87\t  - id: AC4\n88\t    criterion: \"printf 'name size\\\\nfoo 1048576\\\\n' | go run ./cmd/numfmt --to=iec --header --field=2 converts only the second field of data lines, matching gnumfmt.\"\n89\t    traces:\n90\t      - R3.1\n91\t      - R3.3\n92\t  - id: AC5\n93\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gnumfmt passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n94\t    traces:\n95\t      - R4.3\n96\t      - R4.4\n97\t  - id: AC6\n98\t    criterion: \"cmd/numfmt compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n99\t    traces:\n100\t      - R1.1\n101\t      - R1.2\n102\t      - R1.3\n103\t      - R1.4\n104\t      - R2.1\n105\t      - R2.2\n106\t      - R2.3\n107\t      - R2.4\n108\t      - R3.1\n109\t      - R3.2\n110\t      - R3.3\n111\t      - R3.4\n112\t      - R4.1\n113\t      - R4.2\n114\t      - R4.3\n115\t      - R4.4\n116\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f9f02c0-673c-46f7-9a7c-de0e1a90a094","uuid":"0e012e87-d4e2-4dde-a12e-c6f3099f8cfb","timestamp":"2026-05-22T22:49:36.891Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5472/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd071-numfmt.yaml","content":"id: srd071-numfmt\ntitle: \"cmd/numfmt: Convert Numbers from/to Human-Readable Strings\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Shell scripts and data pipelines use numfmt to convert numbers between raw numeric values\n  and human-readable formats with SI or IEC suffixes (e.g., 1K, 1Ki, 1M). macOS has no\n  built-in numfmt command. GNU numfmt from coreutils supports input and output format\n  conversion, field selection, padding, and header skipping. The Go implementation must\n  match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gnumfmt, installed by coreutils) in output and\n  exit codes for all supported flag combinations, verified by differential testing via\n  pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Convert numbers between raw numeric and human-readable formats.\n  - G2: Support SI and IEC suffix conventions for both input and output.\n  - G3: Support field selection, padding, and header skipping for tabular data.\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against gnumfmt via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior and output conversion\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: \"When given --to=UNIT, must convert each input number to a human-readable string with the appropriate suffix. UNIT is one of: si (powers of 1000), iec (powers of 1024), iec-i (powers of 1024 with 'i' suffix), or none.\"\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"When given --from=UNIT, must interpret each input number as a human-readable string with suffixes and convert to a raw number. UNIT values are the same as --to.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: When neither --from nor --to is given, must pass numbers through unchanged.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must read numbers from stdin (one per line) when no operands are given, or process command-line operands directly.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Format control\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"--format=FORMAT must use a printf-style format string for output (e.g., '%10f', '%.2f'). Must support width, precision, and left-alignment.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"--padding=N must pad the output to N characters. Positive N right-aligns; negative N left-aligns.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"--round=METHOD must control rounding: up (ceiling), down (floor), from-zero (away from zero), towards-zero (truncation), or nearest (default).\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"--suffix=SUFFIX must append SUFFIX to the output after the numeric value and any unit suffix.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Field selection and header\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"--field=FIELDS must convert only the specified fields (1-indexed, comma-separated ranges like cut). Other fields are passed through unchanged.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"-d DELIM or --delimiter=DELIM must use DELIM as the field delimiter for --field processing.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: \"--header[=N] must pass through the first N lines (default 1) without conversion, treating them as headers.\"\n      - R3.4:\n          text: \"--to-unit=N must scale the output by dividing by N before applying --to conversion. --from-unit=N must scale the input by multiplying by N before applying --from conversion.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all conversions complete successfully.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: Must exit 2 when an invalid number is encountered (unless --invalid=ignore or --invalid=warn is set).\n      - R4.3:\n          text: \"Differential tests must compare stdout and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils.\"\n      - R4.4:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: --to si/iec/iec-i, --from si/iec, --format with width and precision, --padding, --round modes, --suffix, --field selection, --delimiter, --header, --to-unit/--from-unit, stdin and operand input, and error cases (invalid number, unknown suffix).\"\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/numfmt does not implement locale-aware digit grouping (e.g., thousands separators).\n  - cmd/numfmt does not implement --grouping.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"echo 1048576 | go run ./cmd/numfmt --to=iec produces '1.0M', matching gnumfmt.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"echo 1K | go run ./cmd/numfmt --from=si produces '1000', matching gnumfmt.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"echo 1500000 | go run ./cmd/numfmt --to=si --format='%10.2f' produces a right-aligned formatted value, matching gnumfmt.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"printf 'name size\\\\nfoo 1048576\\\\n' | go run ./cmd/numfmt --to=iec --header --field=2 converts only the second field of data lines, matching gnumfmt.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gnumfmt passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n    traces:\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/numfmt compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n","numLines":116,"startLine":1,"totalLines":116}}}
